// ============================================================
// flow_runtime - shared runtime for the #flow{} effects DSL
// ============================================================
//
// flow is a tiny generator/coroutine language: a `gen` yields values via the
// Yield algebraic effect; a `func` drives a generator with `for x in g(...) {}`,
// which lowers to a `handle` that resumes the generator after each value. This
// is the thing C and Lisp structurally can't say - a generator that SUSPENDS
// mid-loop and RESUMES, carrying its locals across the yield.
//
// The Yield effect is declared ONCE here (an included stdlib, like
// lisp_runtime.lang) so multiple #flow{} blocks in one program share it rather
// than each re-declaring it. Yield(i64) i64: takes the yielded value, the
// resume hands back an i64 (the flow driver ignores it).

include "std/core.lang"

effect Yield(i64) i64
